# BRAZILIAN JIU-JITSU

Version 1.0

---

# Purpose

This document defines the physiological, biomechanical, technical and tactical demands of Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu (BJJ).

Its purpose is to enable the Combat Athlete System (CAS) to understand the unique performance profile of BJJ athletes and to individualize physical preparation accordingly.

This document describes performance requirements.

It does not prescribe training methods.

---

# Definition

Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is a grappling combat sport focused on positional control and submission through joint locks and chokeholds.

Success depends upon:

Control.

Leverage.

Position.

Timing.

Grip management.

Patience.

Technical precision.

---

# Philosophy

Brazilian Jiu-Jitsu is a sport of efficiency.

The objective is not to overpower the opponent.

The objective is to progressively limit the opponent's options while creating increasingly advantageous positions.

Technique should allow a smaller athlete to control a stronger opponent.

